# `this.items = [];`: a field stored through `this` is expected to hold what the checker says of the stored value, and an empty literal is typed never[]. Of what the list will hold that says nothing.
# Taken at its word, an element read in a loop was expected to be undefined, and the read off the true element stood on a rare road.
# f3 = longest
